cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its numerical outputs, cite this v0.2.0 release. The companion manuscript remains an author-review draft."
title: "PhyRoute: Voltage Screening under Feeder Reconfiguration"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: '2026-09-22'
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abhinav0905/phyroute"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Abhinav
    given-names: Kumar
abstract: >
  Code and numerical outputs for comparing neural, physics-only and hybrid
  voltage screening on a balanced IEEE 33-bus feeder. The revised experiment
  evaluates 59 radial branch exchanges, with 15 development and 44 held-out
  exchanges, three training/calibration runs, three test draws and nine verifier
  variants. It generates 1,830,000 topology-scenario cases and retains explicit
  masks for 2,315 numerically unresolved references. Results quantify unsafe
  approvals, false rejections and exact-solver calls. The physics-augmented
  residual model uses additional development-topology training labels, so its
  comparison does not isolate architecture or physics-feature effects.
  Includes frozen protocol records, non-pickle model arrays, independent
  calibration, numerical audits and SVProc LaTeX manuscript sources. The
  companion manuscript is an author-review draft and has not been submitted
  to the conference; affiliation and contact details remain unconfirmed.
keywords:
  - voltage screening
  - power flow
  - feeder reconfiguration
  - verifier mismatch
  - surrogate models
  - adaptive inference
  - reproducible research
